    "text": "The aliphatic <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is sufficiently basic to accept <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> from <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> group in glycine, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> . The <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is not strong enough to donate <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> to the weakly basic aromatic <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in p-aminobenzoic acid, <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/04fdd905-cc09-4497-94a7-723265b5a3cd.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.75in;height:0.56667in\" /> The <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is a sufficiently strong acid to donate <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> to weakly basic aromatic <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> .<br 